\begin{proof}
    This is now an immediate consequence of our construction: The Pl\"ucker clusters differ from the initial cluster $\X_{Q_\infty}$ of $\Sigma_{Q_\infty}$ only in finitely many variables. Hence, 
    by \cite[Prop. 6]{Scott}, any Pl\"ucker cluster $\tilde{\X}$ can be reached from $\X_{Q_\infty}$ by a finite mutation sequence, corresponding to a finite sequence of geometric exchanges (see Figure \ref{fig:geometricex}) of $\Gamma_\infty$.
\end{proof}

