\subsection{Extensions of the algebra $H$}

Now, using the algorithm for constructing solvable Leibniz algebras, we derive all possible extensions of the solvable Leibniz algebra $H$
by the one-dimensional abelian algebra $\mathfrak{h}=\{e_4\}$.
The condition \eqref{c3}, to the linear maps $l,r: H \rightarrow \operatorname{End}(\mathfrak{h})$ such that
$$\begin{array}{ll}l_{x_1}(e_{4})=\alpha_1 e_{4}, & r_{x_1}(e_{4})=\alpha_2e_{4},\\[1mm]
