\section{Processing of Epigenomic Data}
\label{app:processingof}
The epigenetic data used in this paper was gathered from the E017-IMR90 dataset of human fetal lung fibroblast cell genes recorded via the ChIP sequencing method. The respective strengths of all considered epigenetic markers at each base pair were extracted for chromosome 9.

The data was downloaded from the Roadmap Epigenomics Project at \url{https://egg2.wustl.edu/roadmap/web_portal/} (see \cite{RoadmapEpigenomicsProject}) in \texttt{.bigwig} format. It was compiled for further analysis by the \texttt{bigWigToBedGraph} executable, obtained from the binary utilities directory of UCSC: \url{http://hgdownload.soe.ucsc.edu/admin/exe/linux.x86_64/} (see \cite{BinaryUtilitiesDirectory}).

As an example, extracting the strengths of the H3K4me1 marker between base pairs $50'000$ and $100'000$ works like this (executed on a Linux or WSL system):

\texttt{./bigWigToBedGraph E017-H3K4me1.pval.signal.bigwig H3K4me1.bedGraph -start=50000 -end=100000}






