A structure $H$ is said to {\em characterize} a set of cuts ${\mathcal C}$ using a property $P$ if the following condition holds. A cut $C\in {\mathcal C}$ if and only if $C$ satisfies property $P$ in $H$.  %There are two main objectives -- 
It is desirable that $H$ is as compact as possible. Moreover, verifying if a given cut $C$ satisfies $P$ in $H$ has to be as time-efficient as possible.

%firstly, the structure must be as compact as possible, and secondly, property $P$ must be verified efficiently.  


