\begin{lemma} \label{lem : n maxflow}
    Suppose graph $G$ %is a directed graph with real edge weights and $G$
    has exactly two $(s,t)$-mincuts -- $\{s\}$ and $V\setminus \{t\}$. There is an algorithm that can compute a second $(s,t)$-mincut in $G$ using ${\mathcal O}(n)$ maximum $(s,t)$-flow computations. 
\end{lemma}
\begin{remark}
The design of the algorithm stated in Lemma \ref{lem : n maxflow} is based on the covering technique of \cite{baswana2023minimum+} (refer to Theorem 3.2 in Section 3 of \cite{baswana2023minimum+}).  
