\begin{definition}[Anchor edge] \label{def : anchor edge}
    For any given maximum $(s,t)$-flow $f$, an edge $e$ is said to be an anchor edge if $e$ contributes to a $(\lambda+1)$ $(s,t)$-cut and $f(e)=0$. 
\end{definition}
