% Since $x \in \overline{C}$, $(s,x)$-mincut is at most $1$ in $G^f$.
% Let $B$ be an $(s,x)$-mincut. Observe that $B$ has capacity at least $1$ in $G^f$ or $B \setminus\{t\}$ is an $(s,t)$-mincut other than $V\setminus \{t\}$ in $G$ by Lemma \ref{lem : alternative maxflow mincut}.
