\subsection*{Experiment 7}

In this experiment, we applied the randomized SINDy algorithm to the Elec2 dataset, a real-world binary classification problem. The objective of the dataset focuses on predicting the direction of electricity price changes (up or down) in New South Wales (NSW), Australia. Comprising 45,312 instances, the dataset includes five features and spans the period from May 7, 1996 to December 5, 1998. \autoref{tab:Elec2_vars} provides a brief description of the variables and further details can be found in \cite{Harries}. The dataset was sourced from Kaggle (\url{https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/yashsharan/the-elec2-dataset}). All features, with the exception of ``day", were pre-normalized to the range of 0 and 1 upon download. To maintain a uniform data scale, the ``day" variable was subsequently normalized using min-max scaling. The class label distribution is shown in \autoref{tab:Elec2_class}.


