In the right panel of Fig.~3 we again show the isocontour lines for the $m_1$ lower bound in the $\delta$ versus $\theta_{23}$ plane.
One can see that they are just slightly modified by the inclusion of flavour coupling and, for example, the absolute minimum value gets 
slightly relaxed from $m_1 \geq 0.89\,{\rm meV}$ to $m_1 \geq 65\,{\rm meV}$. The most remarkable difference is that now the
excluded region by the cosmological upper bound Eq.~(\ref{upperbm1}), in red in Fig.~3, gets reduced and first octant values of $\theta_{23}$
are now possible also for values $\delta \sim \pi$. For these values of $\delta$, one has that values of the atmospheric mixing angle 
$\theta_{23} \gtrsim 47^\circ$ are still excluded even when flavour coupling is included. In particular, one can see how the best fit point
falls now in the green region that is the one opened by the muonic solutions induced by the account of flavour coupling.   

