   \begin{align*}
\times
\frac{(q^{3^\beta};q^{3^\beta})_\infty^2 (q^{2\cdot2^{2\alpha +1}\cdot 3^\beta};q^{2\cdot2^{2\alpha +1}\cdot 3^\beta})_\infty}
    {(q^{2\cdot 3^\beta};q^{2\cdot 3^\beta})_\infty (q^{2^{2\alpha +1}\cdot 3^{\beta}};q^{2^{2\alpha +1}\cdot 3^{\beta}})_\infty^2}
   \end{align*}

   Since $2^{2\alpha +1}+1\equiv 0\pmod 3$ and $2^{2\alpha +1}+2\not\equiv 0\pmod 3$, collecting the terms involving $q^{3n}$ from both sides of (\ref{th3e4}) and replacing $q^3$ by $q$,and then using (\ref{6}) we have



